"Gods feed on mortals' experience, proficiency and deeds; all of it returns to them at death."
"A noteworthy life is a feast to the gods, and a spectacular death is a fine course."
"Hostile monsters exist in part to push mortals to level, fattening the gods' harvest."
"The gods hate anyone who interrupts one of their harvests."
"A god made the demon labyrinth a trial ground and claims the souls of those who die there."
"That god makes the monsters around the labyrinth attack its outposts ruthlessly."
"Gramps is the Grandfather of Traits: he runs reincarnation and designs traits."
"Gramps made the trait Chimeric Mimicry himself, and gave Syl her Sub-Cores."
"Gramps once smote Simon, the Dreadlich of the crypt dungeon near Southbrook."
"Gramps has threatened to erase those who break his work."
"Gramps warns that those who dig beneath the surface of magic end up killing themselves."
"Mother is the Mother of Magic, and the enchanting system is partly her work."
"Mother guards magic as her life's work and would not let any race ruin it."
"Mother hides subquests inside her quests, like a trojan horse."
"Mother paid for the skill [Skill Deconstruct] out of her own resources."
"Mother preapproved [Mana Dominion], which strips the System's limiters from mana."
"Mother is more generous than Gramps; she seems to discount magic skills for her favourites."
"Qhilleeqeth, the spider queen who rules a dungeon and a race, is Mother's minion."
"Unc is a lesser god, once the Dungeon Master of a jellyfish dungeon, later promoted."
"Unc stutters, claims many friends, and has few; he hates bullying."
"Unc hands out achievements, an old System the other gods thought had been scrapped."
"The Artificer profession is a beta the gods have not yet revealed to the world."
"Gramps, Mother and Unc are allied now, an alliance built on bribes and tricks."
"Gramps and Mother once tied Unc to a chair and gagged him to watch a fight in peace."
"Syl named the gods Gramps, Mother and Unc, and the gods now use those names."
"Unc oversaw the Abyssal Temple dungeon and let its master bully his Experiment Leon."
"Unc named that fled master Gloto, the shadow octopus called Great Lord of the Ocean."
"Syl usurped Gloto's [Dungeon Master] Emblem, but her claim is stuck as pending."
"It is pending because Unc wants to supervise Syl's dungeon and Gramps refuses him."
"Skills seem to be guided magic, a tutorial the System builds for those who cannot weave mana."
"Some knowledge is barred: its names come out garbled, as with [Skill Deconstruct]."
"Dungeon cores were made by the powers behind the System; the CORE is an outdated model."
"Its successor, the Dungeon CUBE, gathers the loose essence of the world for a master."
"Spirits control the world's essence, much as Dungeon Masters do."
"Traz called Syl a doppelganger before Syl and her personas slew him in the Abyss labyrinth."
"The labyrinth's caretaker is the ghost of a withered ancient general or emperor."
"The caretaker ghost reports to superiors and makes the challenge harder for returners."
